Stand up a new Andurel project

Details:
  - Quick Start, also printed by andurel new and in the generated README: andurel tool sync; pnpm install (or bun/npm to match --ui); cp .env.example .env and set the required values; andurel db create (only if the database does not exist); andurel db migrate up; andurel doctor; andurel run; andurel verify.
  - Pass --harness codex|claude|pi|opencode|crush (comma-separated or repeated) to install the bundled agent skill during creation. Without it the skill is not installed and the next steps print an explicit install example.

When to use:
  - Create a new application directory from the current scaffold.
  - Creation is offline: it installs no dependencies and needs no database.

When not to use:
  - Do not run inside an existing Andurel project.

Usage:
  andurel new [project-name] [flags]

Examples:
  andurel new myapp
  andurel new myapp --ui vue/pnpm
  andurel new myapp --harness claude
  andurel new myapp --dry-run --json

Next:
  - cd <project>
  - andurel tool sync
  - pnpm install (or bun/npm install to match --ui)
  - cp .env.example .env
  - andurel db create (only if the database does not exist)
  - andurel db migrate up
  - andurel doctor
  - andurel run
  - andurel verify

Flags:
      --diff              Include a text diff preview in structured output
      --dry-run           Preview project files without creating them
      --harness strings   Install the Andurel skill for these harnesses: codex, claude, pi, opencode, crush (comma-separated or repeated)
  -h, --help              help for new
      --ui string         UI combination: react|vue|svelte / pnpm|bun|npm (default: react/pnpm) (default "react/pnpm")
Global Flags:
      --agent       Emit structured output optimized for agents
      --count       Emit one raw resource count when supported
      --ids-only    Emit one resource identifier per line when supported
      --jq string   Select a field path (for example .routes[0].name) from command data and emit JSON directly
      --json        Emit JSON output
      --md          Emit Markdown output
      --quiet       Suppress non-essential human output
      --verbose     Emit verbose output
